Quantities, Units and Symbols in Physical Chemistry — IUPAC Green Book (@gc-green: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gc-sources) { r_5SR8CP04E580VSV69MYQNSZ73F
Christopher M. A. Brett and fellow editors for IUPAC. Quantities, Units and Symbols in Physical Chemistry, 4th edition, abridged version. Royal Society of Chemistry, 2023. DOI 10.1039/9781839163180. [IUPAC edition page](https://iupac.org/what-we-do/books/greenbook/) · [Official PDF released March 2025](https://iupac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/IUPAC-GB4Abridged.pdf).

Read the complete abridged volume during advanced study, returning to the precise quantity definitions for amount, composition, chemical potential, activity, equilibrium, kinetics, and electrochemistry. Distinguish a quantity equation from an equation valid only for particular numerical units. The available PDF has 122 file pages. Its constants table explicitly uses CODATA 2018 information; consult current evaluated constants when a precision claim needs them rather than calling every table value the latest.

IUPAC supplies authorized free PDF access; preserve the actual RSC/IUPAC edition and component notices before reproducing or adapting material. Free access is stated separately from a general redistribution licence. Edition, editors, release information, contents, and availability checked on 29 October 2026. No copy is bundled.

**Return:** [General chemistry sources — books, courses, data, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_37CHT3QSMD33JDMXE59S6M2ME3).
